WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Five blocks have to go on a chip.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.400
Write each lower-left corner: ten numbers.

3
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.550
Two rows of letters are enough.

4
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:22.210
Change a coordinate and blocks may pile up.

5
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:27.010
Change the letters and nothing ever overlaps.

6
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.610
That is the sequence pair.

7
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.600
Take two blocks; look at their order in each row.

8
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.800
Same order: the first one is on the left.

9
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.400
Opposite: the one first in pos is below.

10
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.780
Five blocks, ten pairs, one relation each.

11
00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.980
Six side by side, four above and below.

12
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:07.350
Left/right forms H; below/above forms V.

13
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:12.350
Each edge: the later block clears the earlier one.

14
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:16.750
Every arrow follows pos, so no cycle.

15
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.560
E must clear A, B, C: candidates 3, 5, 7.

16
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.960
Take the maximum: x = 7.

17
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.700
D clears four blocks: the tallest, B, lifts it to 3.

18
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:36.700
9 × 4, inside the outline.

19
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.900
Three blocks: B must clear both A and C.

20
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:50.900
With the minimum, 2, B sits on A.

21
00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.900
With the maximum, 3, both hold.

22
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:03.181
Identical rows: five blocks in one line.

23
00:02:03.181 --> 00:02:06.648
12 wide: it does not fit 10 × 8.

24
00:02:06.648 --> 00:02:10.337
Reversed: 10 tall, no fit either.

25
00:02:10.337 --> 00:02:13.337
Valid only means no overlap.

26
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.160
Floorplanners search among these encodings.

27
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.500
Change one letter and the packing may not move.

28
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:34.500
D top-left, E bottom-right: both relations hold.

29
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:41.500
14,400 encodings, only 9,056 packings.

30
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:49.500
Which changes really move a block?

31
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.600
In the lab below, edit the two rows yourself.
